BITFIELDS(2)           BIT FIELD MANIPULATION FUNCTIONS            BITFIELDS(2)NAME       bitfields - manipulation of bit fieldsSYNOPSIS       #include bitfields.f83       bitfields ( -- )       +pos ( bits -- pos) private       +width ( bits -- width) private       field ( width -- ) private       bitfield.type ( -- )       bit ( -- )       bits ( width -- )       nibble ( -- )       byte ( -- )       word ( -- )       bitfield.end ( -- )       .field ( field -- )       mask ( width -- mask) private       get ( x field -- y)       put ( x y field -- z)DESCRIPTION       Allows definition and manipulation of bit fields. The bit field       is described in a syntax similar to a structure with fields       from least significant bit towards most significant bit.bitfields ( -- )       Vocabulary for bit field definitions.+pos ( bits -- pos) private       Access field for address of pos(ition) in a named bit field. The        position is stored as a long number.+width ( bits -- width) private       Access field name to address the width of a named bit field. The       width is stored as a long number.bitfield.type ( -- )       Used as:               bitfield.type <bitfield-type-name>                 <bitfield-layout>                    bitfield.end       and then               bitfield.type <instance-name>       Starts the definition of a bit field layout. The bits within       the bit field are numbered from 0 to 31 starting from right (lsb)       to left (msb).bits ( width -- )       Used within a bit field type definitions to give an access name       to a number of bits with in a long number. Used as:               <width> bits <bitfield-name>       within a bit field type definition.field ( width -- ) private       Utility function to create additional constant bit field type       names, other than "bit" etc.    bit ( -- ) private       Used as:               bit <bitfield-name>       within a bit field type definition to give name to a bit at the       current position. The bit positions are numbered from 0 to 31        and right to left within a long number.nibble ( -- )       Used as:               nibble <bitfield-name>       within a bit field type definition to give name to a nibble,        four bits.byte ( -- )       Used as:               byte <bitfield-name>       within a bit field type definition to give name to a byte,        eight bits.word ( -- )       Used as:               word <bitfield-name>       within a bit field type definition to give name to a word,       sixteen bits.bitfield.end ( -- )       Ends the definition of a bit field type. Will give a warning       message if the last field position exceeded 32 bits..field ( field -- )       Prints information about a field; position and width.mask ( width -- mask) private       Utility function to create a mask of a given width. get ( x field -- y)       Given a bit field name, "field", and a long value, "x", the bit        field is accessed and return.put ( x y field -- z)       Given a new value, "x", of a field name, "field", the value "y" is        is updated and returned. The new value is masked to fit the field.SEE ALSO       forth(1)COPYING       Copyright (C) 1989 Mikael R.K. Patel       Permission is granted to make and distribute verbatim copies       of this manual provided the copyright notice and this permission       notice are preserved on all copies.       Permission is granted to copy and distribute modified versions       of this manual under the conditions for verbatim copying,        provided also that the section entitled "GNU General Public       License" is included exactly as in the original, and provided       that the entire resulting derived work is distributed under       the terms of a permission notice identical to this one.       Permission is granted to copy and distribute translations of       this manu